      <!-- SECTION 08: MODEL REFERENCES -->
      <div>
        <div class="sec-hdr" onclick="toggleSec(this)">
          <span class="sec-num">08</span><span class="sec-ttl">Model References</span><span class="sec-tog">v</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sec-body">
          <p class="hint" style="line-height:1.75">
            <strong>Soft-string T&amp;D:</strong> Johancsik, Friesen &amp; Dawson (1984), JPT 36(6), SPE-11380-PA;
            Sheppard, Wick &amp; Burgess (1987), SPE Drilling Eng. 2(4), SPE-15463-PA.<br>
            <strong>Sinusoidal buckling onset:</strong> Dawson &amp; Paslay (1984), JPT 36(10), SPE-11167-PA
            (F<sub>sin</sub> = 2&radic;(EIw&middot;sin&theta;/r<sub>c</sub>)); near-vertical (&lt;3&deg;):
            Lubinski (1950), API Drill. &amp; Prod. Practice (F &asymp; 1.94(EIw&sup2;)<sup>1/3</sup>).<br>
            <strong>Helical onset:</strong> Chen, Lin &amp; Cheatham (1990), JPT 42(2), SPE-19176-PA
            (&radic;2&times;F<sub>sin</sub>) or Wu &amp; Juvkam-Wold (1993), ASME JERT 115 (1.83&times;F<sub>sin</sub>)
            — selectable in Global Parameters.<br>
            <strong>Buckled wall contact:</strong> Mitchell (1986), SPE Drilling Eng. 1(6), SPE-13064-PA
            (N<sub>h</sub> = r<sub>c</sub>F&sup2;/4EI per unit length), applied where compression exceeds the
            helical limit; this drives slack-off lock-up.<br>
            <strong>Model limits:</strong> Mitchell &amp; Samuel (2009), SPE Drill. &amp; Compl. 24(1), SPE-105068-PA.
            <strong>Constants &amp; survey method:</strong> Mitchell &amp; Miska (2011), Fundamentals of Drilling
            Engineering, SPE Textbook Vol. 12 (E = 206.8 GPa); minimum curvature per Sawaryn &amp; Thorogood (2005),
            SPE-84246-PA.<br>
            <strong>Combined motion:</strong> when tripping with rotation, wall friction is resolved along the
            resultant sliding velocity — axial drag &times; v<sub>a</sub>/|v|, torque &times; v<sub>t</sub>/|v|,
            v<sub>t</sub> = &pi;&middot;OD&middot;RPM — per Samuel (2010), SPE-128059-MS and Mitchell &amp; Samuel
            (2009); sliding without rotation carries Torque at Bit to surface unchanged.<br>
            <strong>Display convention:</strong> side force normalized per WellPlan "Contact Force Normalization
            Length" (default 9.45 m = one Range 2 drill-pipe joint).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- RUN -->
      <div style="padding:12px">
        <button class="btn btn-run" onclick="runModel()">RUN T&amp;D MODEL</button>
      </div>

